    "body": "## Objective\n\nCreate an end-user procurement guide under content/docs/user-guide/enterprise/ that explains how to move from a reviewed design to a costed, supplier-ready package.\n\n## Cover\n\n- BOM and supplier candidate inspection.\n- Stock, eligibility, MOQ, order multiples, price tiers, quantities, delivery, and budget inputs.\n- Part assignment/substitution review and procurement lock.\n- Cost snapshot reload and revision binding.\n- Blockers caused by unresolved suppliers, stale quotes, incomplete evidence, or failed checks.\n- Exact PCB supplier/JLCPCB handoff boundary: what Synth prepares, what the external portal does, and whether Synth places no order.\n\n## Screenshot deliverables\n\nProvide 12–16 screenshots for BOM, candidate evidence, review-gated assignment, frozen snapshot, cost report, blocked release, and handoff/confirmation states. Use safe supplier data, redact credentials/order IDs where needed, add alt text/captions, and verify mobile crops.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nNo page claims an order was placed unless that is actually supported; every gate and required human action is explicit; docs link to artifact/review terminology and pass build/preview checks.",
